This repository is a clean rewrite of the local MCP server from
cos-codex-bridge, originally published by Aninvieve Labs (AV-Labs-Co):

  https://github.com/AV-Labs-Co/cos-codex-bridge

The original project is licensed under the MIT License. The license text
is in the LICENSE file and must be retained.

Ideas carried forward from that project:

- a local stdio MCP process, with no hosted endpoint
- realpath allowlists that reject the filesystem root and the home directory
- private on-disk receipts written atomically with mode 0600
- prompts passed to the coding agent on stdin rather than in argv
- the rule that an accepted or queued receipt is not proof of completion

The Codex session runner, git worktree isolation, auto-fix loop, tool
schemas, and this documentation were written again for a Codex-only bridge.
Routes for any coding agent other than the Codex CLI were not carried forward.

This bridge does not deploy or publish. npm publish is disabled by
"private": true, and the registry workflow always exits with an error.
